{{/*
  investigate-report — the shape of the **Investigation Report** produced by
  both investigation prompts (beads-issues/investigate and
  beads/investigate-all-more ("Investigate ALL more")). The report is the
  deliverable that later gets written back into the bead's description /
  acceptance / design fields and posted as a `bd comment`, so both prompts
  must produce the same sections.

  Parameters (dict):
    Target    — the bead ID, or the empty string for the "current problem"
                fallback (only beads-issues/investigate uses the empty
                case). Multi-bead callers pass the literal `<bead-id>`.
    SubIssues — when truthy, adds the "Recommended sub-issues" bullet. Only
                prompts that are allowed to decompose a bead set this.

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/investigate-report" (dict
          "Target" $target "SubIssues" true) }}
*/}}
{{- if .Target }}
### Bead: `{{ .Target }}` — `<Title>`
{{- else }}
### Current problem — `<Topic>`
{{- end }}

- **Clarified problem & scope**: a tightened statement of what this bead or current problem covers,
  and — just as important — what is **out of scope**.
- **Findings & code locations**: key files/symbols and current behaviour, with evidence.
- **Approach**: the recommended step-by-step plan, in order, with the concrete call sites to touch.
- **Refined acceptance criteria**: specific, testable conditions for "done".
- **Design notes**: trade-offs and constraints behind the approach (if applicable).
- **Edge cases & risks**: what could break or is easy to miss — callers, tests, migrations, config.
- **Resolved questions**: the answers settled while investigating.
{{- if .SubIssues }}
- **Recommended sub-issues** (only if the complexity assessment says split): for each, a **title**,
  one-line scope, type/priority, and any dependency on a sibling.
{{- end }}
